    {
      "id": "28d0cf5e-fe1d-5e94-b48b-dccbd36be899",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -704,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 736,
        "height": 1360,
        "content": "## Flag the records where two systems of record disagree\n\nTwo systems that should hold the same records drift apart quietly, and nobody notices until a\ncustomer does. This workflow compares a database table against an API every night, decides which\ndisagreements matter, and marks those records for a human.\n\n### How it works\nOne side is read with a SQL query you write, the other from an HTTP endpoint. Compare Datasets\nlines them up on a key column and sorts every record into four piles.\n\nFields you list as noise are dropped before anything is counted. Without that step a timestamp the\ntwo systems write independently disagrees on every row, and the report is ignored within a week.\n\nWhat survives is triaged. A record whose **critical** fields disagree is flagged in the database\nwith a needs-review column and escalated to your channel straight away, naming the fields and both\nvalues. Everything else waits for the once-a-day digest.\n\nNothing is ever overwritten. The workflow does not decide which side is right, because only a\nperson knows that. It decides which rows a person must look at, which is the part that does not\nscale by hand. There is no model in it: two values are either equal or they are not.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect a Postgres credential and a Slack credential.\n2. Put your SQL query on **Read The Database Side** and your endpoint on **Read The API Side**.\n3. On **Split Out The API Records**, name the field holding the record array, for example data.\n4. On **Line Them Up**, set the key column that identifies the same record on both sides.\n5. Open **Drift Rules** and set **compare_fields**: both sides must return the same field\n   names, and anything outside that list is ignored."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5be46d38-fa69-56fe-bed5-58d39598ea54",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        208,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1056,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 1. Read both sides\nYour SQL query on one side, your endpoint on the other. The HTTP call retries\nbefore the run gives up on it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "011e73a4-7dc2-5f74-a4ed-8fa9b5d479f1",
      "name": "Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1440,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 576,
        "height": 464,
        "content": "## 2. Line them up\nCompare Datasets sorts every record into four piles. Cast database numerics in\nyour SQL, or 20.00 and 20 read as a difference on every row."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "077ce7eb-1b5f-5d5b-80cd-0b9fc834b841",
      "name": "Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2192,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 352,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## 3. Label the drift\nEach pile is labelled with what it is: fields that differ, missing from the\nAPI, missing from the database."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d6a4c2ed-24d8-55c0-a052-2dc36ef5005e",
      "name": "Section 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2720,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 832,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 4. Triage what matters\nFields you list as noise are dropped before anything is counted, so a\ntimestamp that always differs never reaches the report."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a3f921f0-41af-593a-b940-1b6b902d2b35",
      "name": "Section 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3728,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 576,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 5. Flag and escalate\nA record whose critical fields disagree is flagged in the database and\nescalated. Nothing is ever written back to the API side."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fdf5786b-ed95-56c8-b0f7-ab19e1c8c28d",
      "name": "Section 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4480,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 832,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 6. One run, one message\nThe three streams are merged before counting, so a reconciliation posts once.\nMissing records are reported only if you asked for them."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
